exercises.solution:
```python
def mse_gradient(X, y, theta):
    n = len(y)
    return 2 / n * X.T @ (X @ theta - y)
```

Each component $j$ is $\frac{2}{n}\sum_i (\mathbf{x}_i^\top\theta - y_i)\,x_{ij}$ — the residuals weighted by feature $j$ — and `X.T @ residuals` computes all of them at once. The finite-difference check in the tests, $\frac{L(\theta + h e_j) - L(\theta - h e_j)}{2h}$, is slow but almost foolproof; use it whenever you derive a gradient by hand.

